---
/** The named-expert page. Carries the Person entity and the hasCredential
 *  licence number. Sources: F-01 to F-06, B-11, B-12, K-08, K-09, K-11. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnswerBox from '../components/AnswerBox.astro';
import Trust from '../components/Trust.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../data/business';
const o = BUSINESS.owner;
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }];
const quickAnswer = 'Valentin Moriel owns and operates Trusted Termite and Pest Solutions in Seminole, Texas. He holds Texas Department of Agriculture licence TPCL 0918482 as a Responsible Certified Applicator in pest control, termite, lawn and weed categories, and has worked in the trade six years.';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Valentin Moriel | Trusted Termite &amp; Pest"
  description="Seminole born, trained at a Terminix-Rentokil branch in El Paso, licensed TPCL 0918482. The person who answers the phone is the person who does the work."
  path="/about/"
  quickAnswer={quickAnswer}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The person doing the work</p>
      <h1>Valentin Moriel</h1>
      <AnswerBox text={quickAnswer} />
      <Trust />

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.2rem">How he got into it</h2>
      <p>
        "About six years ago, I was recruited by my former district manager from a previous job to become
        the Operations Manager of a small pest control branch. I came into the industry from a management
        and operations background, and because of the position I stepped into, it really became a fast
        track for me to learn and grow in the industry. I wasn't only learning pest control — I was
        involved in virtually every side of the operation, from managing technicians and working directly
        with customers to solving difficult pest problems, sales, training, and the day-to-day operation
        of the branch."
      </p>
      <p>
        That was in El Paso, across two branches including Terminix-Rentokil, over six years. It gave him
        both sides of the job — the technical side and the business side — and it gave him a clear view
        of what large-scale pest control does well and what it does badly.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.2rem">Why Seminole</h2>
      <p>
        Because he is from here. He grew up in Seminole and graduated high school here, and has been in
        and out of Gaines County his whole life. Trusted Termite and Pest Solutions started in November
        2025, and it is deliberately a one-man operation: the person who picks up the phone is the person
        who shows up, inspects the property and does the treatment.
      </p>
      <p>
        On what he took away from working at scale: "Big companies can make customers feel like just
        another number. You get passed around, put on hold, and rarely talk to the same person twice.
        That's actually the environment I came from, and it helped shape what I <em>didn't</em> want my
        company to become. We want to know our customers, take the time to understand their concerns,
        and service their property correctly — not rush through a timed service just to get to the next
        stop."
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:2.2rem">Licence and credentials</h2>
      <ul class="tight">
        <li>Texas Department of Agriculture Structural Pest Control Licence <strong>TPCL {o.tpcl}</strong></li>
        <li>{o.licenceClass}</li>
        <li>Licensed categories: {o.categories.join(', ')}</li>
        <li>Insured — {BUSINESS.insurance.carrier}, $500,000 bodily injury and property damage, $1,000,000 aggregate</li>
        <li>{o.yearsInTrade} years in the trade</li>
        <li>Fluent in English and Spanish</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-3);font-size:.95rem">
        Texas requires a licence number on written estimates. Very few pest control companies in West
        Texas publish theirs anywhere else. You can verify it with the Texas Department of Agriculture.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Cta />
</BaseLayout>
